  era: "Section 24 \xB7 Rise of Nationalism \xB7 1850s \u2013 1910s"
  title: Partition of Bengal
  text: Lord Curzon partitioned Bengal in 1905, officially for administrative reasons, but it was widely seen as a move to divide Hindus and Muslims and weaken nationalism. Mass protests forced its reversal in 1911.
